.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10312:### 0119 — Go's `invalid GOTOOLCHAIN %q` diagnostics quote the environment setting, not the go.mod name — so recognising that lead plus any tail fabricates verdicts
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10314:- FINDING: `TASK-260728-1g0z69` review cycle 7. In `cmd/go/internal/toolchain/select.go`, three `base.Fatalf` sites render `invalid GOTOOLCHAIN %q` while *interpreting the environment setting*, before `go.mod` is read — `:155` (`…: invalid minimum toolchain %q`), `:157`, `:163` (`…: only version suffixes are +auto and +path`). All three quote `gotoolchain` = the env value. Under `GOTOOLCHAIN=local+path` none is reachable at all (`min` is `local`; the suffix is `path`). Only `:198` (`invalid toolchain %q in %s`), `:282` (`invalid GOTOOLCHAIN %q`, after `gotoolchain` is reassigned from go.mod at `:171`/`:208`) and `:351` (`cannot find %q in PATH`) quote a go.mod-derived name. Verified on Go 1.25.1 and 1.25.5.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10315:- ROOT CAUSE: the boundary probe's `toolchain` classifier recognised the exact `invalid GOTOOLCHAIN "v"` form *and* `HasPrefix(line, "invalid GOTOOLCHAIN \"v\":")`. That prefix is not one upstream outcome; it is every message upstream might later render behind that lead, none of them measured. It answered `rejected` — and for any value the isolated `gover` measurement already rejects, the fabricated verdict *agrees*, so the isolated-vs-command crosscheck compared equal and the row stayed green.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10318:- FIX: recognition is a finite list of whole diagnostic lines *predicted before the command runs* from the value under test plus probe-fixed constants (module file name, directive line number, `GOTOOLCHAIN` setting, the probed toolchain's own local version). New measured `classifier closure` section — 331 checks per toolchain over real unrelated command failures, cross-fed measured outcomes, and measured diagnostics structurally extended. New expected-red `-red open-classifier` restores the four retired families: 9 direction-A + 15 direction-B laundered fabrications per toolchain.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10357:- FINDING: requiring the echoed name is load-bearing beyond this defect. `Select` renders two further `invalid GOTOOLCHAIN %q` messages quoting the *environment* value (`local+path`), never the `go.mod` name; those correctly fall to unknown.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10374:- FINDING: the `toolchain`-directive cross-check initializes the command result as accepted and leaves every unrecognized non-zero outcome accepted (`.temp/TASK-260728-1g0z69/probe/main.go:489-500`). Only `invalid toolchain`, `invalid GOTOOLCHAIN`, `cannot find`, and shape rejection are classified explicitly.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10438:- FINDING: `go 1.99.0` is accepted by `GoVersionRE` and `gover.Parse`; on both Go 1.25.1 and 1.25.5, `go mod edit -json` exits 0 while `GOTOOLCHAIN=local go mod tidy` exits 1 only because the running host is too old (`go.mod requires go >= 1.99.0`). The probe would therefore mark a valid compared value as upstream-rejected and falsely fail P1.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10487:- FINDING: the `toolchain` directive's semantic layer can be probed **offline** with `GOTOOLCHAIN=local+path` — a representable name yields `cannot find "X" in PATH`, an unrepresentable one yields `invalid toolchain "X" in go.mod` before any lookup. No download, no installed toolchain needed.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-1jafds/TASK-260728-1jafds_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260728-6a2bde.log:10489:- DECISION: alignment with an ecosystem grammar cannot be stated as set equality when a security partition subtracts from it. Upstream accepts `go1.21.0-custom`; Curator forbids custom-distribution names. Split into P1 `C ⊆ Upstream` (no widening) and P2 `Upstream \ F ⊆ C` (no narrowing outside the forbidden partition), giving `C = Upstream \ F`. `F` is neither a subset of nor disjoint from `Upstream`, so only `C` is pinned.
