pendencies for Go CLI commands, with later closed drivers for other languages. This is a genuine architecture decision, not settled board decomposition. Produce an architecture-only decision packet; do not edit product, spec, schema, code, tests, release metadata, or existing decision documents. Resolve: (1) manifest schema shape for a named external Git build repository and immutable revision/lock semantics; (2) repository-root descriptor name, schema version, target selection, monorepo build_root/source_dir rules, and backward compatibility; (3) exact access behavior: syntax-only offline warning, install/audit hard failure when inaccessible, credential ownership, allowed Git transports, local operator substitutions, moved refs, submodules, LFS, symlinks and special files; (4) snapshot and audit equivalence to in-skill source, including compiler-visible root, dependency graph containment, source identity, receipts, marker v2 and protected cache; (5) deterministic build, install, PATH/shim verification and rollback; (6) platform-owned signing policy and the boundary between local signing and release-time notarization; (7) the extension rule for future Rust, Swift, Kotlin/JVM, C/C++, .NET and other closed drivers; (8) exact impact on existing spec, Curator, cocoaskills and interoperability tasks, while Linux remains a separate later native validation. Explicitly reconcile the user proposal that the repository descriptor name the final binary and output location with the accepted protocol rule forbidding package-controlled executable names and output selection. Prefer logical target IDs plus manager-derived command name and private staging path unless evidence supports another closed design. Audit must happen before any compiler execution. Repository access failure must warn during offline/static check when verification cannot be attempted and must fail install before mutation when source cannot be resolved. Credentials and signing identities must never come from the 