Homebrew/winget/Gradle wrapper/GOTOOLCHAIN.\n\nKey load-bearing property: a version constraint can only filter the manager-trusted set, never add a candidate. Effective requirement is a gate, not a build input (same reasoning that excluded capability evidence in decision 0006); no bypass because Stage A precedes cache lookup. Result: zero frozen artifacts change and adopting the contract causes no rebuild. Go costs no new process - Stage A reuses the three existing package-independent bootstrap probes, so the five Go argument-vector forms stay five and manager-worker-v1 is untouched.\n\nStated asymmetry: a descriptor requirement is unreadable at Stage A because the descriptor arrives with the repository, so Stage A gates on baseline INTERSECT manifest and the descriptor requirement joins at Stage B. That is why the consuming-manifest requirement is REQUIRED in the next schema.\n\nGates, standalone, real exit codes - validate 0 (42 schemas / 422 vector files, before and after), python unittest 0 (29 tests), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0 no output, git diff --check 0, generate-vectors 0. Regenerated conformance/v1 and release/1.0.0-rc.5.json are byte-identical to the accepted predecessor. Clean git-init probe: regenerate-check x2 = 0, release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 = 0. Two negative probes expected-red and red: retired descriptor stem in the new doc rejected by validate (exit 1), broken local link in decision 0007 rejected by validate (exit 1); both reverted, final validate 0. Note: make regenerate-check cannot pass inside the task worktree because it diffs against 57c1f56 while the rc.5 candidate is uncommitted - determinism proven by predecessor byte-comparison and the clean probe instead.\n\nDeliberately not done: no protocol/profile/SECURITY/schema/vector change (TASK-260728-2jaw7h), no schema version numbers (TASK-260728-2spy93), no README release-table row (would falsely claim the design is part of the rc.5 specification set), and no invented probe argv or norm