ax_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-af7289)\nDelivered decision 0007 (canonical) plus docs/compiled-build-toolchain-requirements.md (implementation-ready reference) and one CHANGELOG bullet, in task worktree /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-1g0z69/curator-spec-worktree. Predecessor TASK-260728-2kp3tv worktree preserved read-only (still 127 dirty entries at 57c1f56). Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned; no platform validation claimed.\n\nContract: toolchain-registry-v1 maps each driver to one primary toolchain plus companions over the closed id set go/rust/swift/kotlin/jdk; go entry complete, rust/swift/kotlin/jdk reserved with a fixed obligation list their own driver decisions must fill on a qualified host. toolchain-requirement-v1 is exactly {id, version} with exact/at_least/range over a canonical major.minor.patch triple; combination is interval intersection (associative, commutative, source-order-independent) and an empty intersection is rejected before the host is probed. Prereleases satisfy nothing and cannot appear in a requirement, because no cross-language prerelease order exists. Resolution admits only manager-bundled or trusted operator config; the forbidden-origin and package-influence lists are exhaustive. Two-stage preflight: Stage A (availability/version/platform) right after manifest parse, before external acquisition, cache lookup and persistent mutation; Stage B (go.mod / Cargo.toml + rust-toolchain.toml / swift-tools-version / selected Kotlin field) after local validation or exact external acquisition and audit, before any cache candidate read or compiler child. Metadata is an assertion, never a selector. Eleven stable build_toolchain_* codes carry a guidance_id only; toolchain-guidance-catalog-v1 is manager-owned, versioned, total (release-gate enforced), primary-source-only, text+URL never a command. No auto-install in v1, named explicitly for rustup/swiftly/sdkman/asdf/mis